[{:db/id 17592186073684 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-88cf76f9-070e-56c7-8184-71a9b98899fe" "question-952e22b6-fb4f-5a48-8331-618041da94da"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073495 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/b4/b43d5a0e0a44e6d418a901dc9fa806079b1b9425fc111640439e4338f8bf0d84.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073685 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3f128125-7113-569b-86a4-d5760981b530" "question-d2247508-110b-59bf-98ca-b9f8903d0d7e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073498 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/dc/dcb89325ddd68043c9edf2f595a7a7d89b3ba078bbb1805af7bea58867f627b6.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $\\color{blue}3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}{3}} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073686 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c07fb2aa-7b2a-5715-9eb3-94df22bf1924" "question-d45976ac-7ef3-56df-943b-d0c55df3d8ce"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073499 :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we are multiplying by $\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}$, we need to split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/65/6584c694fbbc990dfa3b58a19545d3deb9889f162da6e02a9820310a190ae04e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](images/e3/e349233ebb5e3927f0d4bda98cb2470c1f17574a522d2f4b9cbddaf365fe946d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073687 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8fb4c868-ce54-5c7d-ab79-c96f1e73ab38"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073500 :question/problem "![](images/82/82439d51448a442dede4b3965ecbbd2f2daa7b2365ea75c80951478fd10af65c.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a9/a95b378064e6ec2ed15637fd05ea49e5f988bfb30d8ae788a7b2086ff920a65f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{4}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac{4}{15}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-88cf76f9-070e-56c7-8184-71a9b98899fe" :question/id #uuid "88cf76f9-070e-56c7-8184-71a9b98899fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-137180" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b7e7ec3356ed3e6eb90075bf8e148b0d3836be7df7551ccac31ffffcb9800ea8.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/50/5091a3f982e94ea27aea26a45b47bf768980dbc802f52905d0ecfc78e111f3ef.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{8}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8eccb805-31a2-5b51-9c68-a40284d36e95"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8eccb805-31a2-5b51-9c68-a40284d36e95" :answer-field/id #uuid "8eccb805-31a2-5b51-9c68-a40284d36e95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f9f51e1e-bfbb-5304-b9d4-16a5cf0b1ad0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-50394559-8014-56