113-569b-86a4-d5760981b530" :question/math-academy-id "q-137402" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c66fe5af6ee7cb43a1327b530027971c60f4b656cd837b305cacafc9cd04307d.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/84/849573cc74dfd2c51479ae3c9c13e8993cfa7cf433887198abda16fe34704eb7.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $2$ equal parts by a horizontal line. So, the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2a5dba11-a208-5184-ace8-45204831aa81"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2a5dba11-a208-5184-ace8-45204831aa81" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a5dba11-a208-5184-ace8-45204831aa81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e7f44dd0-6611-5eea-bf7f-a9815cc649f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7f44dd0-6611-5eea-bf7f-a9815cc649f5" "answer-c4a31fbd-5b49-5328-a37e-224c355fff82" "answer-22a7310b-913f-55c7-b182-39be76669a94" "answer-55309ed7-4c44-5ddb-8208-db7b76f9384b" "answer-60fb4716-8b36-5682-9810-2a38551a2744"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7f44dd0-6611-5eea-bf7f-a9815cc649f5" :answer/id #uuid "e7f44dd0-6611-5eea-bf7f-a9815cc649f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4a31fbd-5b49-5328-a37e-224c355fff82" :answer/id #uuid "c4a31fbd-5b49-5328-a37e-224c355fff82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22a7310b-913f-55c7-b182-39be76669a94" :answer/id #uuid "22a7310b-913f-55c7-b182-39be76669a94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55309ed7-4c44-5ddb-8208-db7b76f9384b" :answer/id #uuid "55309ed7-4c44-5ddb-8208-db7b76f9384b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60fb4716-8b36-5682-9810-2a38551a2744" :answer/id #uuid "60fb4716-8b36-5682-9810-2a38551a2744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d2247508-110b-59bf-98ca-b9f8903d0d7e" :question/id #uuid "d2247508-110b-59bf-98ca-b9f8903d0d7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-210510" :question/problem "Insert the missing number in the multiplication problem below.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"3\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$\\times $</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{4}{6}$ on the left and $\\frac{4}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/54/54e0c1ae73fdf546507c8a4f486f911f1ef8f6bfb57da249a1654393a63151b4.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $4$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $4$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{4}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-07ce1a07-8871-5911-9c9b-077bc1a1b66c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07ce1a07-8871-5911-9c9b-077bc1a1b66c" :answer-field/id #uuid "07ce1a07-8871-5911-9c9b-077bc1a1b66c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a6c98757-3c97-5200-a7f2-0a0514d46039" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6c98757-3c97-5200-a7f2-0a0514d46039"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6c98757-3c97-5200-a7f2-0a0514d46039" :answer/id #uuid "a6c98757-3c97-5200-a7f2-0a0514d46039" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c07fb2aa-7b2a-5715-9eb3-94df22bf1924" :question/id #uuid "c07fb2aa-7b2a-5715-9eb3-94df22bf1924" :question/math-academy-id "q-137425" :question/problem "![](images/31/3167905fdd4699c03f0db5f70f21dc7512a4d24bec7918f3b040259e5c618f5b.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?" :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\frac{1}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/02/0205f15c05454f0d98ae4bbc4c0c8598cbcff880115390a5887a277ceb3f1c4a.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{1}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](images/6a/6a483cf94baee1222f043c2807b23b0249281b8a22f190a6cc311312c677ac07.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8a198355-1ace-51d6-add6-fa89a4dc5132"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8a198355-1ace-51d6-add6-fa89a4dc5132" :an